  "limitations": [
    "This is a bounded SQLx manifest/FFI/source composition and SQLite fix review, not a full Geph/app binary, installed product, broker/account or cross-architecture runtime acceptance.",
    "The three Rust spike tests used a fresh small-project lock (including cc 1.11.1), not the production Geph lock (cc 1.6.0). Production lock metadata resolved on both macOS targets; its compiled qualification remains required.",
    "The C regression invokes the real internal WAL function in unmodified full amalgamations with a deterministic synthetic VFS. It is not an end-to-end malicious database exploit.",
    "Lexical FFI inventory includes optional code and verifies used declarations/constants after documented normalization; it does not establish a complete ABI, memory-safety or side-channel proof.",
    "Bundled SQLite 3.54.1 removes SQLITE_ENABLE_MEMORY_MANAGEMENT from its default flags. SQLx 0.8.6 does not call the affected release-memory/heap-limit APIs; no claim of globally identical engine behavior.",
    "No system SQLite, SQLCipher or environment-based native override is admitted by this review. Exact compiled artifact, current full registry/native dependency admission and ordinary release qualification remain mandatory.",
    "The original three source-owned package descriptors and Rust runtime bytes are unchanged. Their 2026-11-10 source review is reused and rebound to this changed SOURCE/lock; historical fixture tests are historical, not rerun.",
    "Previous BODY_ALLOCATION, BW_CANCELLATION, ENTROPY_ABORT, SECRET_COPIES, NO_ROOT_MODE, KEY_POLICY, CRYPTO_ASSURANCE, SQLITE_PROVENANCE and LICENSE_SCOPE limitations remain; no blanket security or license assurance is added.",
    "The actual local DB/WAL advisory prerequisite is retained. This change removes the vulnerable bundled engine rather than assuming a local database cannot be tampered with.",
    "The expiry remains 2026-12-10 under the previously selected bounded policy; source, lock or package changes invalidate this binding. No automatic renewal or advisory exception."
  ],
